            <ArticleTitle>[Myocardial infarction caused by the thrombosis of the common trunk of the left coronary artery. Fatal outcome despite an early obstruction removal by angioplasty. Apropos of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1551-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an exceptional case of acute myocardial infarction due to thrombosis of the left main coronary artery in a 39-year old male patient. After failure of recanalization by systemic fibrinolysis, percutaneous angioplasty under circulatory assistance was successfully performed pending a possible transplantation. The patient unfortunately died of haemodynamic disturbances 48 hours after the infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
